deletions and reloads. Listing uses creation order. Repeated completion succeeds
unchanged. Completing/deleting an absent ID returns `Error::NotFound(id)`.

Each operation reloads storage; missing storage means an empty collection.
Mutations return success only after replacing the JSON file using a temporary
file in the same directory. Corrupt JSON and filesystem errors are returned;
they never silently reset an existing collection. JSON contains `next_id` and
`tasks`. Concurrent writers and crash/power-loss durability are outside scope.

`cargo run --example lifecycle` exercises the default path through the public API.
Run it only in a disposable project copy with no existing `tasks.json`.
